---
title: M-Ranked — MAX collection sequence
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Scheduler
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant M as MAX adapter
    participant MAX as MAX User API
    participant P as Canonical pipeline
    participant R as Redis

    S->>R: Acquire max partition lease
    S->>DB: Start collection_run and load enabled MAX accounts
    loop For each account within controlled concurrency
        S->>M: collect(account, persistent session reference)
        M->>M: Ensure authorized session&#59; session file mode 0600
        alt Native chat ID is known
            M->>MAX: get_chat(chatId)
        else First resolution
            M->>MAX: join_channel(canonical URL)
        end
        MAX-->>M: Channel identity, title and participant count
        M->>MAX: fetch_history(backward up to 100)
        MAX-->>M: Recent messages and view statistics
        M->>MAX: get_reactions(chatId, messageIds)
        MAX-->>M: Reaction totals and breakdown
        M->>DB: Load bounded circular tracked page + refresh cursor
        M->>M: Select due rows absent from discovery, capped independently
        opt Due historical IDs exist
            M->>MAX: get_messages(chatId, IDs)
            MAX-->>M: Existing messages
            M->>MAX: get_reactions(chatId, returned IDs)
            MAX-->>M: Reaction totals and breakdown
        end
        M->>P: Channel, messages, counters and missing probes
        P->>P: Normalize message type, repost, views and reactions
        P->>P: Keep unsupported comments/shares as NULL, never zero
        P->>P: Confirm only repeated omissions from successful exact get_messages
        P->>DB: Transactional metadata, snapshots, probes and refresh cursor
        DB-->>P: Commit with dataset revision
        P->>R: Publish revision.changed after commit
        P->>DB: Complete account result
        opt Session/network exception
            M->>M: Close runtime and mark disconnected
            M->>DB: Store sanitized failure&#59; reconnect next cycle
        end
    end
    S->>DB: Complete collection_run
    S->>R: Release/expire lease

    Note over M,MAX: MAX uses a user session, not a stable public server API&#59;<br/>credentials/session are secrets and never enter raw payload or logs.
    Note over P,DB: Platform capability is versioned because fields exposed by MAX may change.
    Note over M,DB: History omission and auth/rate/transport failures never increment missing.
